<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#dong-son-culture">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Đông Sơn culture</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1000 BCE–1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> · Also known as Dong Son culture</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Đông Sơn culture was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> culture of the Red River and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ma-river">Ma River</a> valleys of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, named after a village in Thanh Hóa province. It is best known for large decorated bronze drums, traded widely across South-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. Historians associate it with the early polities of Văn Lang and Âu Lạc.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dong-son-culture.jpg" alt="Đông Sơn culture" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bình Giang · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dong_Son_axe.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
